  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=2x-3$, $g(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $h(x)=x^2+1$.\n\nSimplify the following, and hence state the domain.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(g(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{x}-3$, $x\\ge0$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=2g(x)-3\\\\f(g(x))&=2\\sqrt{x}-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe square root requires $x\\ge0$. The domain is $[0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$g(f(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{2x-3}$, $x\\ge\\dfrac32$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(f(x))&=\\sqrt{f(x)}\\\\g(f(x))&=\\sqrt{2x-3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe square-root argument must be nonnegative:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-3&\\ge0\\\\x&\\ge\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain is $[\\frac32,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$h(f(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4x^2-12x+10$, $x\\in\\mathbb R$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}h(f(x))&=(2x-3)^2+1\\\\h(f(x))&=4x^2-12x+9+1\\\\h(f(x))&=4x^2-12x+10\\end{align*}$$\nBoth functions are defined for every real input. The domain is $\\mathbb R$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$g(h(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{x^2+1}$, $x\\in\\mathbb R$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(h(x))&=\\sqrt{h(x)}\\\\g(h(x))&=\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x^2+1\\ge1$ for every real $x$, the square root is always defined. The domain is $\\mathbb R$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
